{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Maintainer intent clarified and recorded: RP-04 is not an authentication, credential-resolution, storage, or refresh subsystem. Rebar is a safe provider-integration host. Upstream SDKs/helpers/CI/deployments own issuance, retrieval, persistence, refresh, rotation, invalidation, and precedence. Rebar owns only safe passage through its seams: fail-closed provider selection, trusted typed provider bindings, operation-scoped construction, exclusion from snapshots/caches/fingerprints/tickets/MCP/CLI/logs/errors, subprocess and adapter isolation, narrow unwrapping of unavoidable static values at the sending adapter, native lifecycle preservation, construction-based close ownership, and non-secret host/account/project policy. The research artifact now uses provider/integration binding as the umbrella concept; RuntimeBindings is explicitly not a credential broker."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786936390188623001,"uuid":"1395c802-81cb-4431-b01d-8fa928766d83"}